rgs\": [\n        \"test\",\nPOSE - validate\n\nExecute the deterministic validation matrix across all modules\n\nUsage:\n  pose validate [--strict|--tolerant] [--stack <s>] [--module <p>] [--report] [--json-out <path>] [--jobs <n>] [--verbose]\n\nDescription:\n  Executes deterministic verification commands (tests, linters, typechecks, builds) declared in .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json.\n\nOptions / Flags:\n  --strict                 Fail on any error or structural validation warning (default in CI)\n  --tolerant               Allow non-blocking warnings while failing on required errors\n  --stack <name>           Filter execution to modules matching the given stack (e.g. go, node, python)\n  --module <path>          Filter execution to a specific module directory path\n  --report                 Persist validation findings into .pose/reports/\n  --json-out <path>        Write structured validation outcome to the specified JSON path\n  --json <path>            Deprecated alias of --json-out <path>\n  --changed-from <rev>     Validate only modules affected between git revisions\n  --jobs <n>               Run up to n checks at once (default: from cores and available memory)\n  --verbose                Stream each check's output as it runs; by default it is captured and a failing check's tail is shown\n\nExamples:\n  $ pose validate --strict\n  $ pose validate --module pose-mcp --verbose\n  $ pose validate --module pose-mcp --strict\n  $ pose validate --json-out .pose/results/delivery-validation.json\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
