{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\n**F1 — medium blocker:** [review_adapter_containment.go:632](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-860956573/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go:632) removes the directory’s name without rechecking its identity after cleaning the opened directory. A concurrent rename and empty replacement can therefore produce successful cleanup despite an identity change, violating R3. The cited regression tests do not exercise this window.\n\nFocused cleanup tests, the containment tests with `-race`, `go vet`, artifact-check and surface-check passed. Both required validation runs failed because the full unit-suite step exceeded 600 seconds; this is not established as a change-specific defect.\n\nApplied the review workflow and Go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence rules. Reviewed bundle `rvb-36a60dc7aca0483b` from the supplied brief. Repository unchanged; no attestation recorded.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go\",\n      \"line\": 632,\n      \"summary\": \"R3 requires identity changes during cleanup to leave cleanup incomplete. Identity is checked only when the build directory is opened at lines 622-625. If that directory is subsequently renamed outside the runtime root and an empty replacement is installed at its original name, removal continues through the original descriptor, root.Remove deletes the replacement, and the outer cleanup can report success while the renamed directory remains. Disappearance is also silently accepted here. Preserve and verify the parent-name binding before confirming cleanup, and add a synchronized regression for replacement after the initial 